WEBVTT

00:03:29.039 --> 00:03:30.600
when we lifted the cylinders:

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:32.469
150 Joules.

00:03:32.469 --> 00:03:35.754
But this time, it took 5 days rather than a minute.

00:03:35.754 --> 00:03:38.830
Five days is 5 times 24

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:40.051
times 60

00:03:40.051 --> 00:03:41.548
times 60 again

00:03:41.548 --> 00:03:44.640
or 432,000 seconds.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:47.048
So we divide the work done by the time

00:03:47.048 --> 00:03:53.231
and find the answer of about 0.00035 Joules per second,

00:03:53.231 --> 00:03:56.791
or about 0.35 milliwatts.

00:03:56.791 --> 00:03:58.719
That's a tiny amount of power.

00:03:58.719 --> 00:04:00.607
This clock uses so little power